    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d414-a1">

                <pb facs="0401" n="319" sameAs="frus:frus1911/pg319"/>

                <p rendition="#center"><hi rendition="#small-caps">declaration.</hi></p>
                <p>In proceeding this day to the signature of the treaty of commerce and navigation
                    between Japan and the United States the undersigned, Japanese ambassador in
                    Washington, duly authorized by his Government, has the honor to declare that the
                    Imperial Japanese Government are fully prepared to maintain with equal
                    effectiveness the limitation and control which they have for the past three
                    years exercised in regulation of the emigration of laborers to the United
                    States.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Y. Uchida.</hi></signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><date calendar="gregorian" when="1911-02-21"
                                ><hi rendition="#small-caps">February</hi> 21,
                        1911</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
